;; WHAT REGEX WORK COSTS.
;;
;; This was Rust's alone. `pike.rs` charged at three sites -- a compile, and
;; the subject of a run and of a find-all -- and NEITHER PORT CHARGED ANYTHING,
;; so a program the native runtime refused on gas ran to completion on the JVM
;; and the CLR. `resource-limits` says the counter is deterministic and proportional; two
;; runtimes out of three were neither.
;;
;; It is here, rather than fixed in each port, because what diverged is the
;; POLICY -- what a compile costs, what a subject costs -- and a policy written
;; three times is a policy that will differ again. The regex functions around
;; it cannot be generated yet (they want array allocation, hole 2), but the
;; price they charge can be, and that price is the whole of the divergence.
;;
;; SEPARATE FROM `pike.kin` for a reason worth knowing: that file's three
;; functions take no receiver, and kin wraps a file in `impl Rt` exactly when
;; it has a method. A file holding both would put the free functions inside
;; the impl, where `pred-hit`'s call to `word-cp` no longer resolves. One
;; receiver-ness per source.
(ns flint.rt.pikegas
  (:require [flint.impl.rt :refer [defn return doc do let charge-work
                                   charge-bytes Rt Value I32]]
            [flint.rt.ropemeas :refer [s-bytes]]))

(doc "What COMPILING a regex program costs: one unit per program word."
     ""
     "CHARGED ON EVERY COMPILE, hit or miss. `matching-over-ropes`: if a compile charged only"
     "on a miss, whether it happened would depend on whether a collection had"
     "run, and the same program would report two different instruction counts"
     "-- exactly the flakiness `resource-limits`'s counter exists to replace."
     ""
     "Answers what it charged, so a test can say so.")
(defn ^:pub ^:method ^I32 charge-compile [^:mut ^Rt rt ^I32 n]
  (do (charge-work rt n)
      (return n)))

(doc "What RUNNING a regex over a subject costs: the subject's BYTES."
     ""
     "Bytes, not code points, and charged BEFORE the walk: the budget has to"
     "bound the work rather than bill for it afterwards, so a pathological"
     "pattern hits the budget rather than the wall clock.")
(defn ^:pub ^:method ^I32 charge-subject [^:mut ^Rt rt ^Value s]
  (let [^I32 n (s-bytes rt s)]
    (do (charge-bytes rt n)
        (return n))))
